\section{Related Work}

\paragraph{Multi-turn jailbreak attacks.}
All multi-turn jailbreak families share a persuasion substrate~\citep{zeng2024pap,hagendorff2026reasoning,li2024mhj}: Crescendo~\citep{russinovich2024crescendo}, FITD~\citep{fitd2024}, DD~\citep{deceptivedelight2024}, and ActorAttack~\citep{ren2024actorattack} each operationalize it differently, while automated methods~\citep{chao2023pair,mehrotra2024tap,perez2022redteaming} iteratively refine prompts and many-shot attacks~\citep{anil2024manyshot} exploit long-context in-context learning. Benchmarks standardize evaluation at single-turn~\citep{mazeika2024harmbench,chao2024jailbreakbench} and multi-turn~\citep{wei2023jailbroken,jiang2024redqueen,song2026multibreak} scales. A detector must generalize across families, not merely succeed on its training distribution.

\paragraph{Multi-turn defenses and production safety.}
No existing defense evaluates cross-attack transfer. Conversation-level systems (DeepContext~\citep{deepcontext2026}, BIID~\citep{tong2025biid}, G-Guard~\citep{gguard2025}, SafeDream~\citep{safedream2026}, JailDAM~\citep{nian2025jaildam}) and representation-level approaches~\citep{lu2025xboundary,zhang2025jbshield,xie2024gradsafe,zou2024circuitbreakers,kulkarni2026latentadversarial,kadali2026trace,hua2026rcs,shen2025antidote,li2025repejailbreak,wang2026trajguard,templeton2024saemitigators} each evaluate on a single family; the latter require white-box access and can be brittle~\citep{derya2026revisitingjbshield}. J-DAPT~\citep{marchiori2025jdapt} applies CORAL-based domain adaptation with cross-modal fusion for multimodal robotic jailbreak detection; our work focuses on text-only multi-turn persuasion attacks and decomposes which adaptation factors drive cross-attack generalization through controlled ablation. Per-turn classifiers~\citep{inan2023llamaguard,metallamaguard3_2024,zeng2024shieldgemma,han2024wildguard,anthropic2025constitutional} and single-turn defenses~\citep{robey2024smoothllm,xu2024safedecoding,jain2023baseline,alon2023perplexity,phute2023selfdefense,hsu2024improved} miss multi-turn trajectories; \citet{li2025m2s} propose converting multi-turn attacks to single-turn for existing guardrails, a complementary approach to our direct multi-turn detection. Our ablation contributes to filling this gap via decomposition across thirteen configurations under OOD evaluation.

\paragraph{Computational persuasion and discourse.}
Persuasion and discourse frameworks~\citep{austin1962speechacts,searle1969speechacts,mann1988rst,prasad2008pdtb,stolcke2000dialogueact} and technique-level classification~\citep{cialdini2001influence,zeng2024pap,hagendorff2026reasoning,dasanmartino2019fine,dasanmartino2020semeval,wang2019persuasion} offer interpretable vocabulary for attacks, but whether such structure aids detection has not been tested. Our ablation shows the taxonomy enables characterization, but detection operates through domain-adapted embeddings regardless of label correctness.

\paragraph{Domain-adaptive pretraining.}
Continued pretraining on domain text yields consistent gains~\citep{gururangan2020dontstop,lee2020biobert,beltagy2019scibert,howard2018ulmfit}, but has not been disentangled for safety-critical generalization. Intermediate-task transfer~\citep{phang2018stilts} and multi-task learning~\citep{caruana1997multitask,liu2019mtdnn} confound domain exposure with supervised signal; our MLM control confirms pretraining alone closes the OOD gap. Dataset artifacts~\citep{gururangan2018artifacts,niven2019probing} motivate TF-IDF, adversarial NLP~\citep{jin2020textfooler,li2020bertattack,nasr2025attackermovessecond,andriushchenko2024adaptive} informs perturbation, and probing~\citep{conneau2018probing,hewitt2019structural} underpins CKA analysis.

